        <mxCell id="c60" value="&lt;i&gt;The register&#x27;s counts for fiscal 2026. Payroll: 26 of its 28 exceptions are the recurring test, open but not unexplained, so the unexplained bar is 2. Purchase orders: the three counts are 8, 8 and 7, because no purchase order exception is expected and only one is reviewed. The bars are counts, not rates; the rates divide each process&#x27;s exceptions by its own documents.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="436" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
